        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-6",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Left anterior knee pain"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Present for approximately 6–8 months; gradual onset without injury. Ache behind and around the kneecap, sometimes a sharp jab with squatting. Worse on stairs, especially descending, with deep squats, and after sitting more than 30–40 minutes. Better with standing or walking on flat ground."
      }
    },
    {
